## Part B — Authentication, Guards & Areas (`api/src/auth/` & `api/src/areas/`)

1. **`GET /api/areas` (`@Public()`)**: returns all areas ordered by `name ASC`.
2. **`POST /api/auth/sign-up` (`@Public()`)**:
   - Validates `SignUpDto` in exact order (`fullName`, `phone`, `email`, `password`, `bloodType`, `areaId`).
   - Checks `AreasService.findByIdOrThrow(dto.areaId)` (`400 Selected area is not supported.`).
   - Checks duplicate `phone` (`409 An account with this phone number is already registered.`) and duplicate `email` (`409 An account with this email address is already registered.`).
   - Hashes password with `bcrypt.hash(dto.password, 10)`.
   - Creates `User` (`role: Role.DONOR`) and `DonorProfile` in a transaction and returns `{ accessToken, user }`.
3. **`POST /api/auth/sign-in` (`@Public()`)**:
   - Looks up user by normalized phone or lowercased email.
   - Compares password with `bcrypt.compare`. If user not found or password mismatch, throws `401 Invalid credentials. Please check your phone/email and password.` (never revealing which part was wrong).
   - If `!user.isActive`, throws `403 This account has been deactivated.`.
   - Signs JWT `{ sub: user.id, role: user.role }` and returns `{ accessToken, user }`.
4. **`GET /api/auth/me`**: returns the authenticated `AuthUser`.
5. **`JwtAuthGuard` & `RolesGuard`**:
   - `JwtAuthGuard` allows `@Public()` endpoints; otherwise verifies the Bearer token and checks `user.isActive === true` (`401 Authentication required. Please sign in.`).
   - `RolesGuard` checks `@Roles(...)` against `req.user.role` (`403 You do not have permission to perform this action.`).

