## Part C — Central Matching & Eligibility Engine (`api/src/matching/matching.service.ts`)

This is the core algorithmic service of the project.

### 1. Red-Cell Compatibility (`R-1`, `R-2`)

| Blood type needed (`request.bloodType`) | Compatible donor blood types (`BLOOD_COMPATIBILITY_MAP`) |
| --- | --- |
| `O-` | `O-` |
| `O+` | `O+`, `O-` |
| `A-` | `A-`, `O-` |
| `A+` | `A+`, `A-`, `O+`, `O-` |
| `B-` | `B-`, `O-` |
| `B+` | `B+`, `B-`, `O+`, `O-` |
| `AB-` | `AB-`, `A-`, `B-`, `O-` |
| `AB+` | `AB+`, `AB-`, `A+`, `A-`, `B+`, `B-`, `O+`, `O-` |

### 2. Rest Period (`R-3`, `R-4`, `R-5`)

- `getNextAllowedDonationDate(lastDonationDate)`:
  - If `lastDonationDate === null`, returns `null` (R-5: a donor with no recorded donation has no rest period).
  - Otherwise adds `REST_PERIOD_DAYS` (`56` days from `common/constants.ts`) to `lastDonationDate` and returns `YYYY-MM-DD` (R-3, R-4).
- `isInRestPeriod(lastDonationDate, now)`:
  - Returns `false` if `lastDonationDate === null`.
  - Returns `true` while `toDateOnlyString(now) < getNextAllowedDonationDate(lastDonationDate)` (R-4). On or after `nextAllowedDonationDate`, returns `false`.

### 3. Single-Donor Eligibility Check (`R-6`, `R-15`, `R-19`)

`checkDonorEligibilityForRequest(donor, request, now)` checks these 5 conditions in order and returns both a `forCoordinator` message (used by `DonationsService`) and a `forDonor` message (used by `PledgesService`):

| Check Order | Condition | Coordinator Message (`POST /donations`) | Donor Message (`POST /pledges`) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `!donor.user.isActive` | `This donor account is deactivated and cannot donate.` | `This account has been deactivated.` |
| 2 | `isInRestPeriod(donor.lastDonationDate, now)` | `This donor is in rest period until YYYY-MM-DD.` | `You cannot pledge while in rest period. Your next allowed donation date is YYYY-MM-DD.` |
| 3 | `!donor.isAvailable` | `This donor is currently marked as unavailable.` | `You cannot pledge while your availability is set to unavailable.` |
| 4 | `!isBloodCompatible(request.bloodType, donor.bloodType)` | `This donor's blood type (<donorType>) is not compatible with <neededType>.` | `Your blood type (<donorType>) is not compatible with this request (<neededType>).` |
| 5 | `donor.areaId !== request.areaId` | `This donor is in <donorArea>, but the request is in <requestArea>.` | `You can only pledge to requests in your registered area (<donorArea>).` |

### 4. Ranked Eligible Donors & Excluded Summary (`R-7`, `R-8`)

`getEligibleDonorsForRequest(requestId)`:

1. Queries all donors in `request.areaId` whose `bloodType` is in `getCompatibleDonorTypes(request.bloodType)`.
2. Classifies each compatible same-area donor:
   - `!donor.user.isActive` → increments `excludedSummary.inactive`
   - `isInRestPeriod(donor.lastDonationDate, now)` → increments `excludedSummary.restPeriod`
   - `!donor.isAvailable` → increments `excludedSummary.unavailable`
   - otherwise → adds to `eligibleDonors`
3. Sorts `eligibleDonors` by:
   - Exact blood-type match (`donor.bloodType === request.bloodType`) first (`true` before `false`)
   - Oldest `lastDonationDate` first (`null` / never donated comes first; then earlier dates before later dates)
   - `fullName` alphabetically (`a.fullName.localeCompare(b.fullName)`)

