## Part A — `RequestsContext` (`client/src/context/RequestsContext.tsx`)

Implement the fixed `RequestsContext` shape (`PROJECT-STRUCTURE.md`, section 5.2):

- `loadSosRequests()`: calls `getSosRequests()` for the public SOS board.
- `loadRequests(filters?)`: calls `getRequests(filters)` for the Coordinator Requests page.
- `loadRequestById(requestId)`: calls `getRequestById(requestId)` for the Request Details page.
- `loadEligibleDonors(requestId)`: calls `getEligibleDonors(requestId)` for the Eligible Donors page.
- `loadAllDonors()`: calls `getAllDonors()` from `donors.api.ts`.
- `createRequest(payload)`: calls `createRequest(payload)`. On success, reloads `loadRequests()` and returns the created request; on failure, saves `mutationError` and returns `null`.
- `updateRequest(requestId, payload)`: calls `updateRequest(requestId, payload)`. On success, reloads `loadRequestById(requestId)` so unit counters, status (`FULFILLED`), and released pledges update immediately without reload.
- `cancelRequest(requestId, payload)`: calls `cancelRequest(requestId, payload)`. On success, reloads `loadRequestById(requestId)`.
- `recordDonation(requestId, payload)`: calls `recordDonation(requestId, payload)`. On success, reloads `loadRequestById(requestId)` (and `loadEligibleDonors(requestId)` if loaded) so collected units, completed/released pledges, and `FULFILLED` status update immediately without reload.

