When all six tasks are merged into `main`, the entire team runs the end-to-end verification on a clean checkout against PostgreSQL (covering Section 6, Section 13, and Section 19 of the specification):

```text
1. Visitor opens Public SOS Board (/) → sees OPEN requests ordered by urgency, with zero personal data.
2. Coordinator signs in (/sign-in) → publishes a new SOS request: A- blood, 3 units, area Homs, urgency CRITICAL (Flow A).
3. Public SOS Board (/) immediately shows the new Homs A- CRITICAL request.
4. Coordinator opens Eligible Donors (/coordinator/requests/:id/eligible-donors) (Flow B) →
   sees only active, available, non-resting A- and O- donors in Homs in the required rank order,
   and sees excludedSummary explaining that Rami (O-, donated 20 days ago) is excluded due to restPeriod.
5. Sara (A-, Homs) signs in (/sign-in) → opens Donor Dashboard (/donor/dashboard) →
   sees ELIGIBLE status and the CRITICAL Homs A- request under "Requests I can help with".
6. Sara clicks Pledge to Donate (Flow C) → her Active Pledge card appears; she tries to pledge to a second request and is rejected (409).
7. Coordinator opens Request Details (/coordinator/requests/:id) → sees Sara's PLEDGED pledge →
   clicks Record Donation for Sara (Flow D).
8. Request now shows 1 of 3 units collected (2 still needed), Sara's pledge is COMPLETED,
   and Sara's dashboard shows she is in REST_PERIOD until 56 days later (and she no longer appears in Eligible Donors).
9. Coordinator records the remaining 2 units from other eligible donors →
   on the 3rd unit, the request automatically becomes FULFILLED, disappears from the Public SOS Board,
   and any remaining PLEDGED pledges become RELEASED.
10. Restart the NestJS backend server → verify all data is still persisted in PostgreSQL.
```

Also verify every item in the **Section 19 Acceptance Checklist**:

* [ ] A donor can sign up, sign in, and see their eligibility status and next allowed donation date.
* [ ] A donor calling a coordinator-only endpoint receives a `403 Forbidden` error.
* [ ] A new request appears on the public SOS board, which shows no personal data.
* [ ] The eligible-donor list for an `A-` request contains only `A-` and `O-` donors from the same area, outside rest period, available and active, in the required order.
* [ ] The excluded-donor summary counts donors excluded for rest period, unavailability, and inactivity.
* [ ] A donor in rest period cannot pledge, and the message gives the next allowed date.
* [ ] A donor with an active pledge cannot pledge again.
* [ ] Recording a donation increases units collected by 1, completes the pledge, and starts the donor's configured rest period (`56` days in this project).
* [ ] Recording the last needed unit marks the request `FULFILLED` and releases remaining pledges.
* [ ] If any step of recording a donation fails, nothing is saved (demonstrated or explained with the `prisma.$transaction` code).
* [ ] `FULFILLED` and `CANCELLED` requests reject updates, pledges, and donations (`409 Conflict`).
* [ ] Data is still there after restarting the backend.
* [ ] Swagger (`/api/docs`) documents every endpoint and its authentication.
* [ ] Meaningful log lines appear in the backend console when a request is created/cancelled/fulfilled and when a donation is recorded or rejected.

