# 18. Final Definition of Done

The project is complete only when all of the following are verified:

### Frontend

* React + TypeScript + React Router + 3 React Contexts (`AuthContext`, `DonorContext`, `RequestsContext`)
* All 8 required screens exist and are reachable through navigation: Public SOS Board (`/`), Sign In (`/sign-in`), Sign Up (`/sign-up`), Donor Dashboard (`/donor/dashboard`), Donor Profile (`/donor/profile`), Coordinator Requests (`/coordinator/requests`), Request Details (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId`), Eligible Donors (`/coordinator/requests/:requestId/eligible-donors`), plus Not Found (`*`)
* Every screen shows loading, empty, and error states with retry
* Forms show backend validation and business-rule rejection messages (such as exact rest-period end date) next to the form
* Lists and unit counters update immediately after an action without a manual page reload
* Protected screens show a clear sign-in prompt when not signed in

### Backend & Database

* NestJS + TypeScript following `Controller → Service → Persistence (Prisma)`
* PostgreSQL database with Prisma schema, migrations, and seed script (areas, >= 2 coordinators, >= 20 donors covering all 8 blood types including resting/unavailable/inactive donors, and requests in `OPEN`, `FULFILLED`, and `CANCELLED` states)
* All data survives a backend restart
* DTO validation on every body, param, and query with `whitelist: true` and `forbidNonWhitelisted: true`
* JWT authentication with `JwtAuthGuard` and `RolesGuard` enforcing `COORDINATOR` and `DONOR` roles
* Swagger / OpenAPI at `/api/docs` documenting every endpoint, parameter, body, and auth requirement
* Custom `AppLogger` logging request created, cancelled, fulfilled, donation recorded, and rejected donation attempts with reason (never logging passwords or tokens)

### Business Rules

* Red-cell blood compatibility (`R-1`, `R-2`) enforced on the backend
* Single configured rest period (`REST_PERIOD_DAYS = 56`, `R-3..R-5`) enforced on the backend
* Eligible-donor matching (`R-6`), ranking (`R-7`), and excluded-donor summary (`R-8`) working accurately
* Request lifecycle (`R-9..R-14`) and pledge rules (`R-15..R-18`) enforced with `400` and `409` errors
* Donation recording (`R-19..R-22`) executed inside a single `prisma.$transaction`, automatically fulfilling the request and releasing remaining pledges when `unitsCollected === unitsRequired`
* Privacy rules (`R-23`, `R-24`) enforced on all public and donor endpoints
* Every team member contributed on their own branches and is ready to present in English
